/-!
# Small certificates for the outer M22 fixed-span bound

Eight order-sixteen sets and the order-thirty-two quintet cover every
sixteen-element commuting set in the native Sylow. Two commuting elements
outside the quintet suffice for coverage: at most twelve partners are
exceptional, and every other pair has its common neighbours in one listed
sixteen-set. Nine independent vectors, each fixed by a nonidentity element,
certify the required span dimension. The matrices act on the literal cocode
modulo the original marked pair line. All certificates are kernel checked.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith H.15.5 and 8.1.3, printed pp.400--401,713--714,
refs/quasithin.pdf. The untrusted generator uses the existing native tables.
-/
